# The weights the anatomy LoRA trains on, on the GPU rental, and nothing else
# (doc/infra.md, GPU rental; ADR-0004 as amended 2026-10-22). Same format and
# rules as models.manifest: this line IS the licence record, and a file with no
# line never loads — the trainer runs with HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1, so ai-toolkit can
# never fetch around it. Kept apart because these ~16 GB run only in training,
# laid out as ai-toolkit reads a local model: klein-base-4b/ is its
# name_or_path, qwen3-4b/ its text encoder.
#
# FLUX.2 [klein] Base 4B in bf16 (Black Forest Labs; Apache-2.0, card and LICENSE.md read 2026-10-29): the undistilled model BFL's guide says to train on, the LoRA then running on the distilled klein-v1.
klein-base-4b/flux-2-klein-base-4b.safetensors  hf:black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-4B/flux-2-klein-base-4b.safetensors  9c5fed22b76baea749d88fc2abe3ad53245e7b21a0d353a762665eea00043b92  Apache-2.0  2026-10-29
# The FLUX.2 VAE (Apache-2.0): the same bytes as the home store's flux2-vae.safetensors and as ai-toolkit/flux2_vae's ae.safetensors (sha256 compared 2026-10-29), under the name ai-toolkit looks for beside the transformer.
klein-base-4b/ae.safetensors  hf:Comfy-Org/vae-text-encorder-for-flux-klein-4b/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors  868fe7b343cc8f3a19dbcfcafbc3d5f888802be3f89bd81b65b3621a066ce8f3  Apache-2.0  2026-10-29
